            new("find", "Find a word in your note", "Use this instead of scrolling through a long document.",
                "Find takes you to matching words without changing them.", "Open a document that contains the word you want to find.",
                "Example: search for meeting in your meeting notes.", "Tern highlights a match and lets you move between matches.",
                "If nothing matches, check spelling and the search options. Search in the current note is different from Find in Workspace, which needs an open folder.",
                [new("Open Find", "Choose Edit → Find…." + Key(CommandIds.Find), "A search field opens for the current document."),
                 new("Enter a word", "Type a word from your note, such as meeting. Use the next/previous match controls.", "The matching text is highlighted."),
                 new("Continue writing", "Close the search controls or return to the writing pane.", "Your note's text is unchanged.")], CommandIds.Find),
            new("save", "Save your work and recognize unsaved changes", "Use this before closing a note or sharing it.",
                "Typing changes the open note. Save writes those changes to a file on your computer, preserving the chosen encoding and line endings. New notes default to CRLF; opening an existing file alone preserves its text.", "Create or open a note. Choose a folder where you are allowed to save files.",
                "Example filename: meeting-notes.md. The .md ending identifies a Markdown text file.", "The file is stored in the folder you chose; the tab no longer shows unsaved changes.",
                "If Save cannot write the file, choose File → Save As… and a writable folder. When closing: Save keeps edits, Don't save discards unsaved edits, and Cancel returns to the note.",
                [new("Save the note", "Choose File → Save." + Key(CommandIds.Save), "A new note asks for a filename and folder; an existing note saves to its current file."),
                 new("Choose a clear filename", "For a new note, enter meeting-notes.md, select your folder and choose Save. Review any overwrite question before agreeing.", "The filename appears on the tab."),
                 new("Check before closing", "After editing again, look for the small colored dot beside the tab name. It marks unsaved changes and disappears after a successful save. Check the file location in the status bar. Save, Save As and Save All preserve your selected LF, CRLF or CR line endings.", "Closing a note never deletes the saved file.")]),
            new("images", "Add a picture to your note", "Use this for a screenshot or a local picture.",
                "The note contains a link to a separate picture file. Keep both together when moving or sharing the editable note.",
                "Choose a writable note. A new note asks where to save, then image insertion continues. Supported pictures are PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP and BMP, up to 16 MiB and 16 million pixels.",
                "![A useful screenshot](assets/screenshot.png)\n\nThe picture file belongs in the assets folder beside your saved note.",
                "An image reference appears in Source and the picture appears in the preview. Save the note to keep the reference.",
                "For a new note, choose a filename in the Save dialog to continue adding the picture; cancelling keeps the draft and inserts nothing. An image file beside the Markdown file is linked immediately through drag-and-drop, Insert Local Image, Ctrl+V or Paste Image as Attachment. For images from other folders, choose Link original to use its existing path or Copy image to choose a separate copy location. Paste Image as Attachment follows the same rules for copied files. Only clipboard pixels without a source file go directly to the copy picker; an existing filename is never overwritten. Undo removes the link but keeps the copied image on disk. If the picture later goes missing, put it back at the linked location or insert it again.",
                [new("Save and choose the insertion point", "Choose File → Save. Return to Split and click the place in the writing pane where the picture belongs.", "The note has a folder, and the caret marks the insertion point."),
                 new("Choose or paste a picture", "Choose Format → Insert Local Image… to use a copied image file, or open the local image picker when no image file is copied. Or select an image file in File Explorer, press Ctrl+C and choose Format → Paste Image as Attachment… in Tern. Copied image pixels work too. Ordinary Ctrl+V pastes images or text; the explicit attachment command needs image data. You can also drag a supported picture into the writing pane.", "All image-file entry points link adjacent files immediately and offer Link original or Copy image for other locations, including Paste Image as Attachment. Clipboard pixels without a source file ask for a copy destination. If the clipboard contains text, ordinary paste inserts that text."),
                 new("Keep the attachment with the note", "Choose a filename inside the note's folder, or a subfolder such as assets. Accept the unique suggested name, check the preview and save the note.", "Your Markdown links to the copied picture using a relative path; the original picture is kept.")], CommandIds.ViewSplit),
            new("pdf", "Make a PDF to share", "Use this when the recipient should read a finished page rather than edit your Markdown.",
                "A PDF is a separate copy. Your editable note remains available.", "Open an existing file or write some text in a new note, then inspect it in Reading or Split. Export HTML, Export PDF and Print stay disabled on a blank new note.",
                "Example: create meeting-notes.pdf while keeping meeting-notes.md for future edits.", "A PDF file is created at the location you choose; your Markdown document stays unchanged.",
                "If the result looks wrong, inspect the preview and try a simpler layout. Some fonts, diagrams or page breaks can differ in PDF. Export again after making a change; an older PDF does not update itself.",
                [new("Review the page", "Choose Reading and check the headings, lists and images.", "You know what you are about to share."),
                 new("Open PDF export", "Choose File → Export as PDF….", "The export window opens; opening it does not overwrite your Markdown."),
                 new("Choose the output", "In Export, choose Browse…, select a separate PDF filename and folder, then choose Export. Open the resulting PDF to check it. The same window also offers HTML page and Plain text.", "You have a separate PDF copy to share.")]),
            new("print", "Print a readable text copy", "Use this when you need a paper copy of the document's text.",
